  "repository": "omacom/omarchy",
  "number": 5140,
  "checked_at": "2026-09-21T11:57:49.070951+00:00",
  "title": "Add WiFi resume hook for T2 MacBooks",
  "author": "fedesapuppo",
  "head_sha": "f25bb1f04be415d5565f6c0c27d7d421906a3170",
  "base_sha": "031ba01c83281f788cb1c1f83d535e6ff84ceda6",
  "base_ref": "dev",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-22T23:31:08Z",
  "state": "open",
  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- Installs a systemd system-sleep hook that reloads the Broadcom WiFi driver after waking from suspend\r\n\r\nThe Broadcom WiFi driver (`brcmfmac`) on T2 MacBooks loses connection state after suspend and silently fails \u2014 WiFi appears connected but can't transmit data. This hook unloads and reloads the kernel module on resume, restoring connectivity.\r\n\r\n## Tested: \r\n\r\n- Run `fix-t2.sh` on a T2 MacBook\r\n- Suspend and resume the machine\r\n- WiFi reconnects automatically after wake",
  "draft": false,
  "files": [
    {
      "sha": "84503abfe4c1cbd20ce754a5dd1a6de63b998b7d",
      "filename": "install/config/hardware/apple/fix-t2.sh",
      "status": "modified",
      "additions": 10,
      "deletions": 0,
      "changes": 10,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/blob/f25bb1f04be415d5565f6c0c27d7d421906a3170/install%2Fconfig%2Fhardware%2Fapple%2Ffix-t2.sh",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/raw/f25bb1f04be415d5565f6c0c27d7d421906a3170/install%2Fconfig%2Fhardware%2Fapple%2Ffix-t2.sh",
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/omacom/omarchy/contents/install%2Fconfig%2Fhardware%2Fapple%2Ffix-t2.sh?ref=f25bb1f04be415d5565f6c0c27d7d421906a3170",
      "patch": "@@ -41,4 +41,14 @@ high_temp=75\n speed_curve=linear\n always_full_speed=false\n EOF\n+\n+  cat <<'HOOK' | sudo tee /usr/lib/systemd/system-sleep/wifi-resume >/dev/null\n+#!/bin/bash\n+if [[ $1 == \"post\" ]]; then\n+  logger -t wifi-resume \"Reloading brcmfmac after resume\"\n+  modprobe -r brcmfmac 2>/dev/null\n+  modprobe brcmfmac || logger -t wifi-resume \"Failed to reload brcmfmac\"\n+fi\n+HOOK\n+  sudo chmod +x /usr/lib/systemd/system-sleep/wifi-resume\n fi"
    },
    {
      "sha": "e101e8ce6c60fb1a1716e27fbf1995282623310a",
      "filename": "migrations/1774703846.sh",
      "status": "added",
      "additions": 13,
      "deletions": 0,
      "changes": 13,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/blob/f25bb1f04be415d5565f6c0c27d7d421906a3170/migrations%2F1774703846.sh",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/raw/f25bb1f04be415d5565f6c0c27d7d421906a3170/migrations%2F1774703846.sh",
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/omacom/omarchy/contents/migrations%2F1774703846.sh?ref=f25bb1f04be415d5565f6c0c27d7d421906a3170",
      "patch": "@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+if lspci -nn | grep -q \"106b:180[12]\" && [[ ! -f /usr/lib/systemd/system-sleep/wifi-resume ]]; then\n+  echo \"Installing WiFi resume hook for T2 MacBook\"\n+\n+  cat <<'HOOK' | sudo tee /usr/lib/systemd/system-sleep/wifi-resume >/dev/null\n+#!/bin/bash\n+if [[ $1 == \"post\" ]]; then\n+  logger -t wifi-resume \"Reloading brcmfmac after resume\"\n+  modprobe -r brcmfmac 2>/dev/null\n+  modprobe brcmfmac || logger -t wifi-resume \"Failed to reload brcmfmac\"\n+fi\n+HOOK\n+  sudo chmod +x /usr/lib/systemd/system-sleep/wifi-resume\n+fi"
    }
  ],
