      "body": "This installs the system-sleep hook into `/usr/lib/systemd/system-sleep`, which is typically reserved for distribution/package-managed units and may be overwritten on upgrades. Elsewhere in this repo, locally-installed systemd artifacts are placed under `/etc/systemd/...` (e.g., `install/config/hardware/apple/fix-suspend-nvme.sh:13`). Consider writing the hook to `/etc/systemd/system-sleep/wifi-resume` instead (and ensure the target directory exists, e.g., via `mkdir -p`).",
